WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.560
In the eight by thirty-two case, the first

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.855
eight lanes read consecutive values. With

00:00:05.855 --> 00:00:08.533
four bytes per value, offsets zero through

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:11.210
seven fit in one aligned thirty-two byte

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:11.593
sector.

00:00:16.093 --> 00:00:18.770
The assignment swaps row and column in the

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.112
output. Will those same lanes store into

00:00:21.112 --> 00:00:22.450
one sector or several?

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.377
After the transpose, adjacent lanes write

00:00:33.377 --> 00:00:36.209
eight words apart. Their offsets are zero,

00:00:36.209 --> 00:00:39.040
eight, and so on, through fifty-six. Each

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.467
falls in a different aligned sector.

00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:48.706
Across all thirty-two lanes, the address

00:00:48.706 --> 00:00:51.445
calculation covers four read sectors and

00:00:51.445 --> 00:00:53.727
thirty-two write sectors. Actual traffic

00:00:53.727 --> 00:00:56.466
also depends on the compiled instructions

00:00:56.466 --> 00:00:57.379
and caches.
